Hallo,

I am quite new to using rkward, but I came up with a question I could 
not answer by research: Is there any way to show some indication of the 
printable space? For example I know other editors which have a grey line 
where A4 paper would end. This would be interesting for me because I 
will be producing larger sequences of R-Code which I will have to print 
out to add to my diploma thesis and I would like to keep the formatting 
as easy as possible.

Thus, my question is if there is any feature in rkward which I haven't 
found yet which may be able to show the printable part of the editor 
window, or indicate where an A4 paper would end.

Thank you very much in advance for any answer.
Best regards,
Sebastian Lerch



From thomas.friedrichsmeier at ruhr-uni-bochum.de  Thu Jun 16 13:48:30 2011
From: thomas.friedrichsmeier at ruhr-uni-bochum.de (Thomas Friedrichsmeier)
Date: 16 Jun 2011 15:48:30 +0200
Subject: [rkward-users] Show A4 Paper dimension
In-Reply-To: <4DF86180.5020806@stud.uni-heidelberg.de>
References: <4DF86180.5020806@stud.uni-heidelberg.de>
Message-ID: <201106161548.30513.thomas.friedrichsmeier@ruhr-uni-bochum.de>

Hi,

On Wednesday 15 June 2011, Sebastian Lerch wrote:
> Thus, my question is if there is any feature in rkward which I haven't
> found yet which may be able to show the printable part of the editor
> window, or indicate where an A4 paper would end.

there is no feature to indicate the printable area. However, I assume you will 
be using a fixed sized font for your code examples, right? So you can:
1) Find out how many chars are printable in your desired font in your word-
processor.
2) Open a script window in RKWard. Select Settings->Configure Editor->Editing. 
Set the static word wrap to the required number of chars, and check the "Show 
static word warp indicator"-option.
Note that this will display an indicator, even if static word wrap is not 
enabled, which is probably just what you are looking for.

Regards
Thomas
